    "slides": [
      {
        "index": 1,
        "text": "It's late at night, and you are quietly finishing slides that were assigned to a struggling colleague.",
        "closing": false,
        "text_tone": "DARK",
        "logo_tone": "DARK",
        "footer_tone": "OLIVE",
        "accent": "OLIVE"
      },
      {
        "index": 2,
        "text": "You tell yourself you're protecting them from management, but your own evening is slipping away again.",
        "closing": false,
        "text_tone": "DARK",
        "logo_tone": "DARK",
        "footer_tone": "OLIVE",
        "accent": "OLIVE"
      },
      {
        "index": 3,
        "text": "You are caught between fearing everything will break and knowing you are breaking yourself to hold it up.",
        "closing": false,
        "text_tone": "DARK",
        "logo_tone": "DARK",
        "footer_tone": "OLIVE",
        "accent": "OLIVE"
      },
      {
        "index": 4,
        "text": "Shielding others from the consequences of their role often prevents them from growing while draining your reserves.",
        "closing": false,
        "text_tone": "DARK",
        "logo_tone": "DARK",
        "footer_tone": "OLIVE",
        "accent": "OLIVE"
      },
      {
        "index": 5,
        "text": "Recognizing where your work ends and theirs begins isn't a failure of support; it's clarity.",
